{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "supro-1624t-dual-tone",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Supro 1624T Dual-Tone",
  "description": "Supro 1624T (Valco, c. 1962) as drawn by ClassicTubeAmps (Ryan), cross-checked against the factory Supro S6424 sheet (same 6973 power amp, paraphase and tremolo, with its voltage chart). Channel 1: .005 uF into a 12AX7 half with a 470K grid leak (and jack 2's 100K), 2200 unbypassed cathode, 270K plate load with 100K/.05 uF decoupling, .005 uF to a 500 kA Volume with a 500 pF bright cap across top-to-wiper, 270K mixer. Channel 2 (the input): .005 uF, 470K and jack 4's 100K, 2200 grid stopper, 1500 || 35 uF cathode shared with the tremolo cathode follower, 270K/100K/.05 uF plate, .005 uF, 270K to ground, .005 uF to its 500 kA Volume (500 pF bright cap), 270K mixer. The mixing node (V2 pin 2) carries 500 pF to ground and the 500 kL Tone (track to ground, wiper to .005 uF). Paraphase: V2A 270K plate, 2200 || .05 uF cathode; .01 uF to the upper 6973, whose 270K grid leak returns through the 12K tap that drives V2B (3900 cathode, 270K plate, .01 uF to the lower 6973 with 470K). Two 6973 beam pentodes in class A: plates on the OT centre tap at the rectifier node, screens on the 1K node, shared 250 Ohm 7 W || 35 uF cathode. Tremolo: third 12AX7, phase-shift oscillator (270K plate, .03/.02/.01 uF ladder with 100K + 500 kL Speed, 1M, 1.5M, 2200 grid stopper, 1000 cathode), .05 uF / 1M / .02 uF, the Speed-pot switch, 2.2M into the 500 kL Intensity rheostat with .05 uF, and a cathode follower whose cathode is channel 2's V1B cathode: the tremolo modulates channel 2's bias. Supply: 5Y3 into 20 uF, 1 kOhm 1 W, 10 uF, 15 kOhm, 10 uF. Re-converted 2026-11-12 (VERIFY_BATCH_3 and the control audit): the previous netlist had no tremolo, a 12k screen dropper (the drawing's 12K is the paraphase tap), the tone on channel 2's volume, the bright caps across the mixers and 100k plate loads.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "ClassicTubeAmps traced Supro 1624T schematic (Ryan): all values and the channel/paraphase topology",
      "url": "https://el34world.com/charts/Schematics/Files/Supro/Supro_1624t_schematic_263.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sluckey Supro 1624T layout (cross-check of topology and pot wiring)",
      "url": "http://sluckeyamps.com/supro/supro.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Supro 1624T Dual-Tone reissue manual (what the reissue's bright and mod controls do; used only to decide which catalogue controls are real)",
      "url": "https://www.suprousa.com/uploads/supro/2020/11/1624T_Dual-Tone_Manual.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Amp Garage thread on original 1624T vs 6424 Dual Tone (grid-leak vs cathode bias, different tone network, split-cathode paraphase)",
      "url": "https://ampgarage.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=29511"
    },
    {
      "title": "Factory Supro Model S6424 schematic with voltage chart (page 5 of the Sluckey S-6424 document): cross-check of every preamp, PI, power and tremolo value",
      "url": "http://sluckeyamps.com/supro/supro.pdf"
    }
  ],
  "io": {
    "input": "in2",
    "output": "spk",
    "inputVoltsPerFS": 1.0,
    "outputVoltsPerFS": 40.264,
    "note": "outputVoltsPerFS 16.964 -> 40.264 (2026-11-12 re-conversion): the drawn preamp (270K plate loads, no 470K input pad) has 7.5 dB more gain at the catalogue defaults; the scale keeps the shipped DI level (6 s Clean Strumming excerpt, --table 152000) at the previous release's 2.376 V-equivalent. Dimed peak speaker voltage 13.86 V (1 V/220 Hz, volume and tone 1): the 1.5x rule would give 20.8; the level policy keeps the shipped loudness instead."
  },
  "oversampling": 2,
  "lte": {"start": "bdf2", "note": "LTE substeps start on BDF2 (docs §10.61). Engine 8x fine-step truth, audio band, lead / rock DI: 0.099 / 0.454 % -> 0.098 / 0.265 %; aliasing -76.1 -> -80.2 dB at 0.5 FS. CPU equal (9900X)"},
  "minRate": 176400,
  "solver": "auto",
